chunks.coverage_notes:
Files read in full: components/machine_tracker/tracker.c, tracker_menu.c, tracker_priv.h; components/machine_radio/radio.c, radio_menu.c, radio_web.c, radio_priv.h. The scope files machine_tracker.h and machine_radio.h do not exist in the tree, so there was nothing to read. I also read the relevant parts of worker.h, machine_core.c (activate/stop ordering), audio.c (how process() is called), menu.c (preset_load order), setup_menu.c (render buffers), clock.h (ppb_eff), and the rest-api /trk/upload handler.

Checked and found safe: the tracker ring flush/load handshake (loading=true plus vTaskDelay(1) before wpos/rpos reset); libxmp frame sizes against the ring size; the retrig index maths (indices are masked by % TRK_RING_FRAMES); ICY metadata buffer bounds; the radio resampler bounds in the normal case; and the worker start/stop lifecycle.

Not verified: real libxmp/helix internals (xmp_start_player failure modes, whether esp_http_client_open() follows redirects in IDF 4.3), because vendored code was out of scope. The 20 KB radio stack under HTTPS was not measured, so I did not report it. The uint32 wpos/rpos wrap after about 27 hours of continuous play (one glitch at the wrap) and torn reads of title/url strings were dropped as not consequential."}
